  "overview": "The Des Moines Police Department uses Flock Safety automated license plate reader technology to support criminal investigations and enhance public safety while maintaining appropriate privacy protections. Authorized personnel may conduct searches following a crime and receive real time alerts involving stolen vehicles, missing or endangered persons, qualifying felony or gross misdemeanor warrants, and vehicles connected to felony or gross misdemeanor investigations.\n\nThe department\u2019s use of this technology is governed by policy, training, access controls, audits, and data retention requirements. It complies with Washington\u2019s Driver Privacy Act, ESSB 6002, and applicable requirements and guidance from the Washington State Attorney General\u2019s Office.\n\nAs part of our commitment to transparency and responsible use, the department has made its policies and usage statistics available below\n\nCommunity Impact\nData & Usage Summary",
  "policy_info": "",
  "alpr_policy": "-Immigration investigations or enforcement, as provided in RCW 10.93.160.\n-Investigations involving protected health care services under Chapter 7.115 RCW.\n-Tracking or otherwise monitoring activity protected by the state and federal constitutions\n\nThe Department shall not collect ALPR data on, immediately surrounding, or providing access to or from:\n-Facilities providing protected health care services.\n-Facilities conducting immigration matters, as defined in RCW 19.154.020.\n-Elementary or secondary schools.\n-Places of worship.\n-Courts.\n-Food banks.\n\nOur entire APLR policy can be found at this link https://www.desmoineswa.gov/departments/police/f_l_o_c_k_transparency_portal",
